{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":494815,"name":"","username":"soulsoup","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/soulsoup/{size}/121369_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-18T09:36:10.713Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494815-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494815-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494815-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494815-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNot able to recover or use my GROK BOT just says trying to recover on my Android Phone. This has been happening since 11 am IST. I tried reinstalling but the setting up of computer is not happening. Just says Can’t reach your computer either I should RETRY or Recover Computer. Both of which is not happening\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494815-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494815-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can try to sign out and sign in it’s still coming like that\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494815-operating-system-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494815-operating-system-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOther\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494815-version-information-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494815-version-information-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIts GROK BOT newest version as I just downloaded it day before yesterday\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494815-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494815-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-18T09:36:21.580Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":38,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":190.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":172128,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-issue-in-android-a-bug-or-some-outage","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":138600,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-issue-in-android-a-bug-or-some-outage/172128/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":494855,"name":"Colin","username":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-18T10:07:33.612Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003cspan class=\"mention\"\u003e@anindya_sinha\u003c/span\u003e, thanks for the report, and sorry for the trouble.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGood news first: your Grok Bot computer and your Bots are fine on our side. Every “Recover computer” you tapped actually completed, and nothing was deleted. What is failing is the phone’s network lookup of the address the app uses to reach your computer. Looking at the timing, the phone worked normally on your home Wi-Fi until about 7:20 AM today, and the trouble started around 10:45 AM once it was on the mobile network it has been on since. Some mobile carriers’ DNS servers do not resolve that address, and reinstalling or recovering cannot change that.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease try this on the phone:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Android Settings and go to Network \u0026amp; internet.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTap Private DNS (on some phones it is under Advanced, or search Settings for “Private DNS”).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eChoose “Private DNS provider hostname” and type: one.one.one.one\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTap Save.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully close Grok Bot (open Recents and swipe it away, or Settings → Apps → Grok Bot → Force stop).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eReopen Grok Bot, sign in if asked, and give it up to two minutes on the setup screen.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you would rather test quickly first, connect the phone to your home Wi-Fi (the one that worked yesterday) instead, then do steps 5 and 6.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-18T10:07:33.612Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":6.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":172128,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-issue-in-android-a-bug-or-some-outage","display_username":"Colin","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Community Support Engineer","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":87436,"hidden":false,"trust_leve